   VULNERABILITY
 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

        CWE-602  client-side enforcement of server-side security
        CWE-321  hard-coded / locally-derivable cryptographic key material
        CWE-327  risky algorithm choice (AES key derived from machine code)
        CWE-345  no authenticity verification (no signature, no MAC)
        CWE-472  plaintext expiry field parsed without validation

        License payload ..: <MachineCode> \t <ExpireDate> [\t <Email>]
        Cipher ...........: AES-128-CBC / PKCS7 / UTF8
        Key derivation ...: Key = f+g+h+e ,  IV = a+c+d+b
                            (8 fixed slices of the 32-char machine code)
        Machine code .....: MD5_HEX(motherboard serial + SALT + CPU id)
        Storage ..........: HKCU\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\<3 letters>\Configuration
                            %APPDATA%\Microsoft\Crypto\Keys\<machine code>
        Decision point ...: a single 'public static int Days' field
        Permanent flag ...: Days >= 29200  (80 years)

        Forging the payload into BOTH storage locations yields a permanent
        license. The "dual-store consistency check" is a formality: writing
        both copies defeats it.

 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
   CLOUD CONTROL REMOVAL
 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

        The vendor re-validates online ~15s after startup. On rejection the
        client rewrites the local license to '<JQM> \t Invalid \t <Email>'
        and calls Environment.Exit(0). A plain forgery survives only ~1-2 min.

        The bundled DLL uses three redundant layers:

          [1] License forgery
              WMI machine-code recompute + AES derivation + dual-store write

          [2] Cloud-control removal
              selective IWebProxy: only the vendor domain is routed to a dead
              port (127.0.0.1:9); all other traffic stays direct

          [3] Memory lock
              watchdog pins App.Days to the permanent threshold every second
              and restores the on-disk license within 5s if rewritten

        Measured: 8+ minutes stable, zero outbound connections,
                  zero license rollback events.

